var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"internal/","page":"BibInternal","text":"BibInternal contains the canonical entry model and the lossless document types used by Bibliography.jl.\n\nThis page exists mainly as a bridge for readers who want to understand how the high-level API maps onto the shared data model.\n\n","title":"BibInternal"},{"category":"module","location":"internal/#BibInternal.BibInternal","page":"BibInternal","text":"BibInternal provides the canonical bibliography model shared by the bibliography stack.\n\nIt keeps the core entry types, validation rules, diagnostics, and lossless document containers in one place so parsers and exporters can share the same data model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.BibInternal"},{"category":"constant","location":"internal/#BibInternal.entries","page":"BibInternal","text":"const entries\n\nList of possible entries (currently based on bibtex). Keep it sorted for readability.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.entries"},{"category":"constant","location":"internal/#BibInternal.fields","page":"BibInternal","text":"const fields = [\n    :address,\n    :annote,\n    :archivePrefix,\n    :author,\n    :booktitle,\n    :chapter,\n    :crossref,\n    :edition,\n    :editor,\n    :eprint,\n    :howpublished,\n    :institution,\n    :isbn,\n    :issn,\n    :journal,\n    :key,\n    :month,\n    :note,\n    :number,\n    :organization,\n    :pages,\n    :primaryClass,\n    :publisher,\n    :school,\n    :series,\n    :title,\n    :type,\n    :volume,\n    :year\n]\n\nList of possible fields (currently based on bibtex). Keep it sorted for readability\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.fields"},{"category":"constant","location":"internal/#BibInternal.maxfieldlength","page":"BibInternal","text":"const maxfieldlength\n\nFor output formatting purpose, for instance, export to BibTeX format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.maxfieldlength"},{"category":"constant","location":"internal/#BibInternal.rules","page":"BibInternal","text":"const rules = Dict([\n    \"article\"       => [\"author\", \"journal\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"book\"          => [(\"author\", \"editor\"), \"publisher\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"booklet\"       => [\"title\"]\n    \"eprint\"        => [\"author\", \"eprint\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"inbook\"        => [(\"author\", \"editor\"), (\"chapter\", \"pages\"), \"publisher\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"incollection\"  => [\"author\", \"booktitle\", \"publisher\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"inproceedings\" => [\"author\", \"booktitle\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"manual\"        => [\"title\"]\n    \"mastersthesis\" => [\"author\", \"school\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"misc\"          => []\n    \"phdthesis\"     => [\"author\", \"school\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"proceedings\"   => [\"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"techreport\"    => [\"author\", \"institution\", \"title\", \"year\"]\n    \"unpublished\"   => [\"author\", \"note\", \"title\"]\n])\n\nList of BibTeX rules bases on the entry type. A field value as a singleton represents a required field. A pair of values represents mutually exclusive required fields.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.rules"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.AbstractBibliographyRule","page":"BibInternal","text":"Base type for declarative and custom bibliography validation rules.\n\nThird-party packages may subtype this type and extend validate_rule without modifying BibInternal's canonical field model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.AbstractBibliographyRule"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.AbstractEntry","page":"BibInternal","text":"Abstract entry supertype.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.AbstractEntry"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Access","page":"BibInternal","text":"struct Access\n    doi::String\n    howpublished::String\n    url::String\nend\n\nStore the online access of an entry as a String. Handles the fields doi and url and the arXiv entries. For additional fields or entries, please fill an issue or make a pull request.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Access"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Access-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibInternal","text":"Access(fields::Fields)\n\nConstruct the online access information based on the entry fields.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Access"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.AlternativeRequiredField","page":"BibInternal","text":"AlternativeRequiredField(names)\n\nA requirement where at least one of the listed fields must be present.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.AlternativeRequiredField"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.BibliographyDocument","page":"BibInternal","text":"BibliographyDocument\n\nLossless document-level container returned by parsers that need to preserve ordering, non-entry blocks, and parse diagnostics.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.BibliographyDocument"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Date","page":"BibInternal","text":"struct Date\n    day::String\n    month::String\n    year::String\nend\n\nStore the date information as day, month, and year.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Date"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Date-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibInternal","text":"Date(fields::Fields)\n\nConstruct the date information based on the entry fields.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Date"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Diagnostic","page":"BibInternal","text":"Diagnostic\n\nStructured message attached to a bibliography document, raw entry, or field. The suggestion field is intentionally textual for now so command line tools and future GUIs can present a friendly next action without depending on a fix engine.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Diagnostic"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.DiagnosticSeverity","page":"BibInternal","text":"@enum DiagnosticSeverity diagnostic_info diagnostic_warning diagnostic_error\n\nSeverity level for structured diagnostics emitted while parsing, normalizing, or validating bibliography data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.DiagnosticSeverity"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Entry","page":"BibInternal","text":"struct Entry <: AbstractEntry\n    access::Access\n    authors::Names\n    booktitle::String\n    date::Date\n    editors::Names\n    eprint::Eprint\n    id::String\n    in::In\n    fields::Dict{String,String}\n    note::String\n    title::String\n    type::String\nend\n\nGeneric Entry type. If some construction rules are required, it should be done beforehand. Check bibtex.jl as the example of rules implementation for BibTeX format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Entry"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Entry-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"BibInternal","text":"Entry(id::String, fields::Fields)\n\nConstruct an entry with a unique id and a list of Fields.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Entry"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.EntryRule","page":"BibInternal","text":"EntryRule\n\nValidation rule for one source entry type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.EntryRule"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.EntryRuleSet","page":"BibInternal","text":"EntryRuleSet\n\nVersioned collection of entry validation rules for a bibliography format. The aliases dictionary applies before entry-specific aliases, which makes it easy to share canonical field names across the whole format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.EntryRuleSet"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Eprint","page":"BibInternal","text":"struct Eprint\n    archive_prefix::String\n    eprint::String\n    primary_class::String\nend\n\nStore the information related to arXiv eprint format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Eprint"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Eprint-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibInternal","text":"Eprint(fields::Fields)\n\nConstruct the eprint arXiv information based on the entry fields. Handle old and current arXiv format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Eprint"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.FieldCardinalityRule","page":"BibInternal","text":"FieldCardinalityRule(name, minimum=0, maximum=nothing)\n\nConstrain the number of values in a structured field. Flat string values count as one; parsers that preserve multiple values should pass a collection.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.FieldCardinalityRule"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.FieldSpec","page":"BibInternal","text":"FieldSpec\n\nFormat-independent description of a canonical bibliography field. Parsers and exporters own source-format mappings; this catalog only describes the semantic field exposed to downstream consumers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.FieldSpec"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.FieldTypeRule","page":"BibInternal","text":"FieldTypeRule(name, value_kind)\n\nRequire a populated field to match a canonical value kind such as :integer, :year, :date, or :uri.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.FieldTypeRule"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Fields","page":"BibInternal","text":"Fields = Dict{String, String}. Stores the fields name => value of an entry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Fields"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.ForbiddenField","page":"BibInternal","text":"ForbiddenField(name)\n\nReject a field when it has a value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.ForbiddenField"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.In","page":"BibInternal","text":"struct In\n    address::String\n    chapter::String\n    edition::String\n    institution::String\n    isbn::String\n    issn:String\n    journal::String\n    number::String\n    organization::String\n    pages::String\n    publisher::String\n    school::String\n    series::String\n    volume::String\nend\n\nStore all the information related to how an entry was published.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.In"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.In-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibInternal","text":"In(fields::Fields)\n\nConstruct the information of how an entry was published based on its fields\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.In"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.LosslessEntry","page":"BibInternal","text":"LosslessEntry\n\nPair a stable canonical Entry with the raw source entry and diagnostics used to build it. This keeps existing consumers on Entry while enabling parsers and writers to preserve source information.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.LosslessEntry"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.MutuallyExclusiveFields","page":"BibInternal","text":"MutuallyExclusiveFields(names)\n\nAllow at most one populated field in the group.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.MutuallyExclusiveFields"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.Name-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibInternal","text":"Name(str::String)\n\nDecompose without ambiguities a name as particle (optional) last, junior (optional), first middle (optional) based on BibTeX possible input. As for BibTeX, the decomposition of a name in the form of first last is also possible, but ambiguities can occur.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.Name"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.RawBlock","page":"BibInternal","text":"RawBlock\n\nTop-level source block that is not necessarily a bibliographic entry, such as a BibTeX comment, preamble, string definition, or free text.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.RawBlock"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.RawEntry","page":"BibInternal","text":"RawEntry\n\nLossless representation of a parsed bibliography entry. kind is the source entry type, key is the citation key when the format has one, and fields preserves source order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.RawEntry"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.RawField","page":"BibInternal","text":"RawField\n\nLossless representation of a parsed field.\n\nname and value contain the interpreted field pair, while raw preserves the source representation. span and diagnostics are optional metadata collected by parsers that keep source locations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.RawField"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.RequiredField","page":"BibInternal","text":"RequiredField(name)\n\nA single required field in an entry rule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.RequiredField"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.RuleContext","page":"BibInternal","text":"RuleContext\n\nContext passed to validate_rule. Custom rule packages can extend validate_rule(rule, fields, context) for their own AbstractBibliographyRule subtype.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.RuleContext"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.RuleProfile","page":"BibInternal","text":"RuleProfile\n\nNamed and versioned set of composable bibliography rules. A nothing supported_entry_types value means that the profile accepts every entry type; it is used for product or institution overlays.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.RuleProfile"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.SourceSpan","page":"BibInternal","text":"SourceSpan\n\nOptional source location for raw bibliography content and diagnostics. The span uses 1-based inclusive coordinates.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.SourceSpan"},{"category":"type","location":"internal/#BibInternal.ValidationResult","page":"BibInternal","text":"ValidationResult\n\nResult of validating one entry or a bibliography document. ok is true when no diagnostic has diagnostic_error severity.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.ValidationResult"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#Base.isless-Tuple{BibInternal.Date, BibInternal.Date}","page":"BibInternal","text":"Base.isless(a::BibInternal.Date,b::BibInternal.Date)::Bool\n\nFunction to check for a < b on BibInternal.Date data types.\n\nThis function will throw an ArgumentError if the year can not parsed into Int. If it is not possible to parse month or day to Int those entries will be silently ignored for comparison. This function will not check if the date fields are given in a correct format all fields are parsed into and compared as Int (no checking if date format is correct or valid!).\n\ndanger: Note:\nThe silent ignoring of not parseable month or day fields will lead to misbehaviour if using comparators like == or !==!\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.isless"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#Base.isless-Tuple{BibInternal.Name, BibInternal.Name}","page":"BibInternal","text":"Base.isless(a::BibInternal.Name,b::BibInternal.Name)::Bool\n\nFunction to check for a < b on BibInternal.Name data types.\n\nThis function will check the fields last, first and middle in this order of priority. The other fields are ignored for now. The field comparison is done by string comparison no advanced alphabetizing rules are used for now.\n\ndanger: Note:\nThe silent ignoring of the other fields might lead to misbehaviour if using comparators like == or !==!\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.isless"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.arxive_url-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibInternal","text":"arxive_url(fields::Fields)\n\nMake an arxiv url from an eprint entry. Work with both old and current arxiv BibTeX format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.arxive_url"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.canonical-Tuple{BibInternal.Entry}","page":"BibInternal","text":"canonical(entry)\n\nReturn the canonical Entry view of an entry-like object.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.canonical"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.canonical_field_specs-Tuple{}","page":"BibInternal","text":"canonical_field_specs()\n\nReturn the canonical field catalog in stable display order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.canonical_field_specs"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.check_entry-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"BibInternal","text":"check_entry(fields::Fields)\n\nCheck the validity of the fields of a BibTeX entry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.check_entry"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.compose_profiles-Tuple{Vararg{BibInternal.RuleProfile}}","page":"BibInternal","text":"compose_profiles(profiles...; name)\n\nCompose format, product, and institution profiles. Constraints accumulate. Conflicts are retained as error diagnostics on the resulting profile rather than being resolved through precedence.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.compose_profiles"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.diagnostics-Tuple{BibInternal.LosslessEntry}","page":"BibInternal","text":"diagnostics(entry)\n\nReturn the diagnostics attached to a lossless entry or document.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.diagnostics"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.entry_fields-Tuple{BibInternal.Entry}","page":"BibInternal","text":"entry_fields(entry::Entry)\n\nConvert a canonical Entry back into a flat field dictionary. This is the bridge used by validation and format conversion code.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.entry_fields"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.erase_spaces-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibInternal","text":"erase_spaces(str::String)\n\nErase extra spaces, i.e. r\"[  ]+\", from str and return a new string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.erase_spaces"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.field_spec-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"BibInternal","text":"field_spec(name)\n\nReturn the canonical specification for name, or nothing for a source-specific extra field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.field_spec"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.get_delete!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"BibInternal","text":"get_delete!(fields::Fields, key::String)\n\nGet the value of a field and delete it afterward.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.get_delete!"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.handle_validation-Tuple{BibInternal.ValidationResult, Any}","page":"BibInternal","text":"handle_validation(result::ValidationResult, level)\n\nApply a validation policy. :error raises on errors, :warn logs warnings, and :none returns the result untouched.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.handle_validation"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.make_biblatex_entry-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"BibInternal","text":"make_biblatex_entry(id::String, fields::Fields; check = :error)\n\nMake an entry using BibLaTeX field aliases and date conventions while preserving source-specific fields that are not part of the canonical view.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.make_biblatex_entry"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.make_bibtex_entry-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"BibInternal","text":"make_bibtex_entry(id::String, fields::Fields)\n\nMake an entry if the entry follows the BibTeX guidelines. Throw an error otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.make_bibtex_entry"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.names-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibInternal","text":"names(str::String)\n\nDecompose into parts a list of names in BibTeX compatible format. That is names separated by and.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.names"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.profile_field_names-Tuple{BibInternal.RuleProfile, AbstractString}","page":"BibInternal","text":"profile_field_names(profile, entry_type)\n\nReturn fields made available by the profile for an entry type. Custom fields remain legal unless a profile explicitly forbids them.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.profile_field_names"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.profile_rules-Tuple{BibInternal.RuleProfile, AbstractString}","page":"BibInternal","text":"profile_rules(profile, entry_type)\n\nReturn global rules followed by rules for the normalized entry type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.profile_rules"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.raw-Tuple{BibInternal.LosslessEntry}","page":"BibInternal","text":"raw(entry)\n\nReturn the raw source representation attached to a lossless entry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.raw"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.space-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibInternal","text":"space(field::Symbol)\n\nReturn the amount of spaces needed to export entries, for instance to BibTeX format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.space"},{"category":"function","location":"internal/#BibInternal.validate","page":"BibInternal","text":"validate(entry::LosslessEntry, ruleset::EntryRuleSet = BIBTEX_RULESET)\n\nValidate the canonical view of a lossless entry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.validate"},{"category":"function","location":"internal/#BibInternal.validate-2","page":"BibInternal","text":"validate(entry::Entry, ruleset::EntryRuleSet = BIBTEX_RULESET)\n\nValidate a canonical entry against a ruleset.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.validate"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.validate-Tuple{BibInternal.BibliographyDocument, BibInternal.EntryRuleSet}","page":"BibInternal","text":"validate(document::BibliographyDocument, ruleset::EntryRuleSet)\n\nValidate every entry stored in a lossless bibliography document.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.validate"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.validate_fields-Tuple{AbstractDict, BibInternal.EntryRuleSet}","page":"BibInternal","text":"validate_fields(fields::AbstractDict, ruleset::EntryRuleSet; id::AbstractString = \"\")\n\nValidate one field dictionary against a ruleset and return structured diagnostics. The input dictionary can come from a parser or from a canonical entry converted back to fields.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.validate_fields"},{"category":"method","location":"internal/#BibInternal.validate_fields-Tuple{AbstractDict, BibInternal.RuleProfile}","page":"BibInternal","text":"validate_fields(fields, profile; id=\"\")\n\nValidate one entry against a composed rule profile.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibInternal.validate_fields"},{"category":"section","location":"","page":"Bibliography","text":"Bibliography is the orchestration layer of the bibliography stack.\n\nUse it when you want a simple API for common operations:\n\nimport a bibliography from BibTeX, BibLaTeX, RIS, CFF, CSL-JSON, EndNote, or MODS;\nvalidate or filter a bibliography document;\nsort entries;\nexport to BibTeX, BibLaTeX, RIS, CFF, CSL-JSON, EndNote, MODS, or a lightweight web projection.\n\nusing Bibliography\n\nbib = read_bibliography(\"references.bib\")\nvalidate(bib)\nselected = select(bib, [\"lovelace1843\"])\nwrite_bibliography(\"references.out.bib\", selected)\n\n","title":"Bibliography"},{"category":"module","location":"#Bibliography.Bibliography","page":"Bibliography","text":"Bibliography is the high-level bibliography interface for the Humans of Julia stack.\n\nIt combines BibParser.jl and BibInternal.jl into a single package that can import, validate, filter, sort, and export bibliographic data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.Bibliography"},{"category":"constant","location":"#Bibliography.sorting_rules","page":"Bibliography","text":"const sorting_rules = Dict{Symbol, Vector{Symbol}}(\n\t\t\t\t:nty  => [:authors; :title; :date],\n\t\t\t\t:nyt  => [:authors; :date; :title],\n\t\t\t\t:nety => [:authors; :editors; :title; :date],\n\t\t\t\t:neyt => [:authors; :editors; :date; :title],\n\n:y    => [:date],     );\n\nImplemented sorting rules for bibliography entry sorting.\n\nSee also sort_bibliography!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.sorting_rules"},{"category":"type","location":"#Bibliography.Publication","page":"Bibliography","text":"Publication\n\nA structure to store all the information necessary for web export.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.Publication"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.Publication-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"Publication(entry)\n\nConstruct a Publication for the lightweight web projection.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.Publication"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.access_to_bibtex!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"access_to_bibtex!(fields, a)\n\nTransform the how-to-access field to a BibTeX string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.access_to_bibtex!"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.bibliography_entries-Tuple{BibInternal.BibliographyDocument}","page":"Bibliography","text":"bibliography_entries(bibliography)\n\nReturn an ordered dictionary of canonical entries keyed by entry id.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.bibliography_entries"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.bibtex_to_web-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"bibtex_to_web(source::String)\n\nConvert a BibTeX file to the lightweight web projection returned by export_web.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.bibtex_to_web"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.cff_dict-Tuple{BibInternal.Entry}","page":"Bibliography","text":"export_cff(e::Entry, destination::String=\"CITATION.cff\", version::String=\"1.2.0\", add_preferred::Bool=true) -> Dict{String, Any}\n\nExport an Entry to a CFF file (default is CITATION.cff).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.cff_dict"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.compose_rule_profiles-Tuple{Symbol, Vararg{BibInternal.RuleProfile}}","page":"Bibliography","text":"compose_rule_profiles(format, overlays...; name)\n\nCompose a destination format profile with product, project, or institution overlays.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.compose_rule_profiles"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.date_to_bibtex!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"date_to_bibtex!(fields, date)\n\nConvert a date to a BibTeX string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.date_to_bibtex!"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.eprint_to_bibtex!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"eprint_to_bibtex!(fields, eprint)\n\nConvert eprint information to a BibTeX string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.eprint_to_bibtex!"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.export_biblatex-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"export_biblatex(bibliography)\n\nExport a bibliography to BibLaTeX format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.export_biblatex"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.export_bibtex-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"export_bibtex(target, bibliography)\n\nExport a bibliography to BibTeX format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.export_bibtex"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.export_bibtex-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"export_bibtex(bibliography)\n\nExport a bibliography to a BibTeX string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.export_bibtex"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.export_bibtex-Tuple{BibInternal.Entry}","page":"Bibliography","text":"export_bibtex(e::Entry)\n\nExport an Entry to a BibTeX string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.export_bibtex"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.export_cff-Tuple{BibInternal.Entry}","page":"Bibliography","text":"export_cff(e::Entry; destination::String = \"CITATION.cff\",\n           version::String = \"1.2.0\", add_preferred::Bool = true)\n\nExport an Entry to a CFF file and return the generated dictionary.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.export_cff"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.export_cff_collection-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"export_cff_collection(bibliography; destination, version=\"1.2.0\",\n                      add_preferred=true) -> Vector{String}\n\nExport every bibliography entry as an independent, specification-compliant CFF document in destination. Files are named <entry-id>.cff; the returned vector contains their paths in bibliography order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.export_cff_collection"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.export_csl-Tuple","page":"Bibliography","text":"export_csl(args...)\n\nPlaceholder for the CSL writer extension. Install the corresponding extension package to enable it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.export_csl"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.export_endnote-Tuple","page":"Bibliography","text":"export_endnote(args...)\n\nPlaceholder for the EndNote writer extension. Install the corresponding extension package to enable it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.export_endnote"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.export_mods-Tuple","page":"Bibliography","text":"export_mods(args...)\n\nPlaceholder for the MODS writer extension. Install the corresponding extension package to enable it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.export_mods"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.export_web-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"export_web(bibliography::DataStructures.OrderedDict{String,BibInternal.Entry})\n\nExport a bibliography in internal format to a lightweight web projection. The same representation is also used by DocumenterCitations.jl.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.export_web"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.field_to_bibtex-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"field_to_bibtex(key, value)\n\nConvert an entry field to BibTeX format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.field_to_bibtex"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.fileio_load-Tuple{FileIO.File{FileIO.DataFormat{:BIB}}}","page":"Bibliography","text":"fileio_load(file; check)\nfileio_load(stream; check)\n\nThe FileIO interface to import a BibTeX file or parse a BibTeX string and convert it to the internal bibliography format. The check keyword argument can be set to :none (or nothing), :warn, or :error to raise appropriate logs.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.fileio_load"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.fileio_save-Tuple{FileIO.File{FileIO.DataFormat{:BIB}}, Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"fileio_save(file, data)\nfileio_save(stream, data)\n\nExport a bibliography as a BibTeX string to a file or stream.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.fileio_save"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.filter_bibliography-Tuple{BibInternal.BibliographyDocument, Function}","page":"Bibliography","text":"filter_bibliography(bibliography, predicate)\n\nFilter entries with predicate(entry), preserving document metadata when the input is a lossless document.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.filter_bibliography"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.import_bibtex-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"import_bibtex(input; check = :none)\n\nImport a BibTeX file or parse a BibTeX string and convert it to the internal bibliography format. The check keyword argument can be set to :none (or nothing), :warn, or :error to raise appropriate logs.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.import_bibtex"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.import_cff-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"import_cff(input; id=\"\") -> Entry\n\nImport a CFF file and convert it to the internal bibliography format.\n\nWhen no identifier is supplied, a deterministic internal identifier is derived from the CFF title and release year. CFF itself has no citation-key field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.import_cff"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.import_cff_collection-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Bibliography","text":"import_cff_collection(source) -> OrderedDict{String, Entry}\n\nImport a collection of independent CFF documents. source can be a directory containing .cff files or a vector of file paths. Each file stem becomes the entry id, making directory export/import round-trips preserve bibliography keys without adding non-standard fields to the CFF documents.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.import_cff_collection"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.in_to_bibtex!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"in_to_bibtex!(fields::BibInternal.Fields, i::BibInternal.In)\n\nConvert the \"published in\" information to a BibTeX string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.in_to_bibtex!"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.int_to_spaces-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"int_to_spaces(n)\n\nMake a string of n spaces.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.int_to_spaces"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.na_if_empty-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Bibliography","text":"na_if_empty(str::AbstractString) -> AbstractString\n\nUse placeholder value if string param is empty.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.na_if_empty"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.name_to_string-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"name_to_string(name::BibInternal.Name)\n\nConvert a name in an Entry to a string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.name_to_string"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.names_to_strings-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"names_to_strings(names)\n\nConvert a collection of names to a BibTeX string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.names_to_strings"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.read_bibliography-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"read_bibliography(input; format = :auto, check = :error)\n\nRead a bibliography from a path, stream, or string and return a lossless BibInternal.BibliographyDocument.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.read_bibliography"},{"category":"function","location":"#Bibliography.recursive_isless","page":"Bibliography","text":"recursive_isless(a::Entry, b::Entry, fields::Tuple{Symbol},\n                 depth::Int = 0)\n\nHelper function for sort_bibliography!.\n\nThis function allows recursive checking if a < b with descending importance. The importance set for the comparison is defined by the argument fields. This argument is a tuple consisting of symbols denoting the fields of the data type BibInternal.Entry. The ordering implies the importance.\n\nThe depth argument is purely for iterating/recursive purposes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.recursive_isless"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.rule_profile-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"Bibliography","text":"rule_profile(format)\n\nReturn the canonical validation profile associated with a supported bibliography format. Exchange-format profiles deliberately validate the canonical input required by the current exporter; source schema validation remains the parser's responsibility.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.rule_profile"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.select-Tuple{OrderedCollections.OrderedDict{String, BibInternal.Entry}, Vector{String}}","page":"Bibliography","text":"select(\n    bibliography::DataStructures.OrderedDict{String,Entry},\n    selection::Vector{String};\n    complementary::Bool = false\n    )\n\nSelect a subset of bibliography entries by key.\n\nIf complementary is true, the keys in selection are excluded instead of kept.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.select"},{"category":"function","location":"#Bibliography.sort_bibliography!","page":"Bibliography","text":"sort_bibliography!(\n    bibliography::DataStructures.OrderedDict{String,Entry},\n    sorting_rule::Symbol = :key\n    )\n\nSorts the bibliography in place.\n\nThe sorting order can be set by specifying the sorting_rule. The sorting is implemented via isless() functions. For detailed insight have a look at the isless() implementation of Julia and BibInternal.jl.\n\nSupported symbols for sorting_rule are:\n\n:key (default): sort by bibliography keys e.g. BibTeX keys or :id\nthe sorting rules defined in sorting_rules\n\ninfo: Note:\nThe sorting is not following explicitly bibliographic alphabetizing conventions. It follows standard comparator behaviour implied by the implemented isless() functions (string comparators).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.sort_bibliography!"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.validate-Tuple{BibInternal.BibliographyDocument}","page":"Bibliography","text":"validate(bibliography; ruleset=nothing, profile=nothing)\n\nValidate a bibliography document or collection of entries and return a BibInternal.ValidationResult. With neither keyword, a document uses its format profile. ruleset remains available for compatibility; new consumers should use composable profile values.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.validate"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.write_bibliography-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"write_bibliography([target], bibliography; format = :BibTeX, mode = :normalized)\n\nWrite or return a bibliography string. With mode = :original or mode = :preserved, a lossless document returns its original source when available. With mode = :normalized, entries are emitted from the canonical view.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.write_bibliography"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.xcite-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"xcite(entry)\n\nFormat the BibTeX cite output of an Entry for web export.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.xcite"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.xfile-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"xfile(entry)\n\nFormat the downloadable path of an Entry file for web export.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.xfile"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.xin-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"xin(entry)\n\nFormat the appears-in field of an Entry for web export.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.xin"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.xlabels-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"xlabels(entry)\n\nFormat the labels of an Entry for web export.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.xlabels"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.xlink-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"xlink(entry)\n\nFormat the download link of an Entry for web export.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.xlink"},{"category":"function","location":"#Bibliography.xnames","page":"Bibliography","text":"xnames(entry, editors = false; names = :full)\n\nFormat the name of an Entry for web export.\n\nArguments:\n\nentry: an entry\neditors: true if the name describes editors\nnames: :full (full names) or :last (last names + first name abbreviation)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.xnames"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.xtitle-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"xtitle(entry\n\nFormat the title of an Entry for web export.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.xtitle"},{"category":"method","location":"#Bibliography.xyear-Tuple{Any}","page":"Bibliography","text":"xyear(entry)\n\nFormat the year of an Entry for web export.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bibliography.xyear"},{"category":"section","location":"parser/","page":"BibParser","text":"BibParser handles the actual source parsing, but Bibliography.jl exposes the same functionality through read_bibliography and write_bibliography.\n\nThis page is intentionally short because the package is meant to feel like a single entry point rather than a parser zoo.\n\n","title":"BibParser"},{"category":"module","location":"parser/#BibParser.BibParser","page":"BibParser","text":"BibParser converts bibliography source formats into BibInternal data.\n\nThe package focuses on parsing only. Use parse_entry and parse_file for the legacy entry dictionary workflow, or parse_bibliography when you want a lossless BibInternal.BibliographyDocument.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.BibParser"},{"category":"method","location":"parser/#BibParser.detect_format-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibParser","text":"detect_format(input)\n\nBest-effort format detection used by parse_bibliography when format = :auto.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.detect_format"},{"category":"method","location":"parser/#BibParser.detect_xml_format-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"BibParser","text":"detect_xml_format(content::AbstractString)\n\nHeuristic XML format detection used by the parser extensions.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.detect_xml_format"},{"category":"method","location":"parser/#BibParser.is_zero-Tuple{Tuple}","page":"BibParser","text":"is_zero(t::Tuple)\n\nExtends iszero as is_zero to Tuple types. Return true iff all elements of t are equal to zero.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.is_zero"},{"category":"method","location":"parser/#BibParser.name_to_string-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibParser","text":"name_to_string(name::BibInternal.Name)\n\nConvert a name in an Entry to a string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.name_to_string"},{"category":"method","location":"parser/#BibParser.occurs_in-Tuple{Any, Char}","page":"BibParser","text":"occurs_in(re, char::Char)\n\nExtends occursin as occurs_in to test if a regular expression re is a match with a Char.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.occurs_in"},{"category":"method","location":"parser/#BibParser.parse_bibliography-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibParser","text":"parse_bibliography(input; format::Symbol = :auto, check = :error)\n\nParse a bibliography and return a BibInternal.BibliographyDocument preserving raw source blocks where the parser supports lossless mode.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.parse_bibliography"},{"category":"method","location":"parser/#BibParser.parse_entry-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibParser","text":"parse_entry(entry::String; parser::Symbol = :BibTeX, check = :error)\n\nParse a single BibTeX entry string using the legacy parser.\n\nFor bibliography formats with validation rules, the check keyword argument can be set to :none, nothing, :warn, or :error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.parse_entry"},{"category":"method","location":"parser/#BibParser.parse_file-Tuple{Any, Val{:BibTeX}}","page":"BibParser","text":"parse_file(path::String, parser::Symbol = :BibTeX; check=:error)\n\nParse a bibliography file and return the legacy entry representation.\n\nThe default parser is :BibTeX. Use :BibLaTeX or :RIS directly in the core package, and install the relevant extensions to enable the other formats. For bibliography formats with validation rules, check can be :none, nothing, :warn, or :error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.parse_file"},{"category":"method","location":"parser/#BibParser.parse_string-Tuple{Any}","page":"BibParser","text":"parse_string(input::String; format::Symbol = :BibTeX, check = :error)\n\nParse bibliography content from a string and return entries in the legacy format. Prefer parse_bibliography when source preservation and diagnostics are needed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"BibParser.parse_string"}]
}
